---
code: artifact-form-fallback
when-fires: the emission planner was left to choose (no `--form`) and settled for a LESS flattened form than the stream posture allowed it to aim at. Minted at the cli's emission-planner edge, spanless, once per run, on the same three causes its refusing sibling carries. `{form}` = what was emitted; `{cause}` = the closed reason word; `{loads}` = how many book-sited load occurrences the cause counted.
why: 30I §7.1: auto aims for the contracted-dependency default and falls toward the preserved book tree WITH an explicit explanation. The pair with `artifact-form-refused` is the whole selector contract — an explicitly named form is never silently downgraded, and an unnamed one never quietly gives up: an admin who does not know their plan is not self-contained finds out on the target. Note severity with no floor: the artifact is valid and safe, and what was lost is flattening. Remediation register (help) wanted: say what the emitted form does NOT carry, and which single change would earn the more flattened one.
---
-- replay --
$ dorc plan --book=book.sh
note[artifact-form-fallback]: [unwritten: artifact-form-fallback]
